.TH XD\-ENDTASK 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-endtask \- the End Program box for a program that isn't responding
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-endtask
.I pid
.I title
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-endtask
is an internal helper of XeonDesktop:
.BR xd\-compositor (1)
runs it when a window that is closed doesn't respond.
It shows Windows' \(lqEnd Program \- \fItitle\fR\(rq box:
End Now kills the process
.I pid
(SIGKILL), losing its unsaved data; Cancel leaves it running.
If the process has gone, or its id now belongs to another user's
process, nothing is killed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 for a bad process id or when there is no Wayland compositor to
show the box on.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-compositor (1),
.BR xd\-taskmgr (1)
